  "limits": "Finite plaintext loopback checks, one host. Timed traffic uses two retained peers before/after population; departure itself is fully verified but paced to preserve default queues. Private scope uses zero listener flags, isolating index scanning from additional listener fanout. Profiles/exploratory runs are excluded from final timing medians. Rehash allocates metadata under the write lock; snapshots are event-boundary RSS, not a process memory cap or page-return guarantee. Fresh private CPU/p99 differ, and ordinary guard changes are retained without a general speed claim. Unpaced departure, larger active application fanout, channel-name table costs, long duration, TLS/proxies, cluster routing and hosted deployment/CI are unverified."
